  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1118 AM CST Fri Nov 27 2026\n\nA Colorado Low is expected to eject from the Rockies tomorrow, \nreaching Middle TN by Sunday morning. This will bring another\nround of widespread rain, and perhaps a few thunderstorms. Rain\nchances start to pick up around sunrise Sunday, maxing out near\n100% in the late morning and early afternoon. During the FROPA,\nmedium range models place SBCAPE around 100 J/kg, which is plenty\nto get a few thunderstorms, but not necessarily supportive of\nsevere weather. In addition, meager PWATs around 1 inch will only\nsupport about a half inch of QPF on Sunday. This will be something\nto watch over the coming days, but it's looking like a run-of-\nthe-mill rainfall event at this time.\n\nMoving into next week, we're looking at dry and progressively\nwarmer conditions Monday through at least Thursday morning due to\nupper level ridging. Temperatures creep up to almost 10 degrees \nabove normal in the mid 60s by Thursday afternoon. Another shot of\nwidespread rain is on tap late week due to a cold front.",
